Appendix F: Statistical Framework and Measurement Models

F.1 Operationalization of Constructs

Originality.  \hat{O}(N) = 1 - \frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}_{\text{known}}|} \sum_{a \in \mathcal{A}_{\text{known}}} \cos\_\text{sim}(\text{embed}(N), \text{embed}(N_a)) 

where embed is a pre-trained sentence encoder (e.g., SBERT, CLIP text encoder). The known attractor narratives  N_a  are collected from a calibration set.

NIV.  \widehat{\text{NIV}}(N)  is computed by a verifier model (possibly ensemble). The verifier outputs a score in  [0, |N|]  approximating the theoretical NIV. Calibration against human annotations yields an estimate of verifier bias and variance.

Diversity. For a set  \mathcal{P} ,  \hat{D}(\mathcal{P}) = \frac{2}{|\mathcal{P}|(|\mathcal{P}|-1)} \sum_{i<j} \hat{d}_c(p_i, p_j)  where  \hat{d}_c  uses the same embedding space plus causal graph edit distance.

F.2 Measurement Error Model

\hat{O}(N) = O(N) + \varepsilon_O, \quad \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_O] = 0

\widehat{\text{NIV}}(N) = \text{NIV}(N) + \varepsilon_{\text{NIV}}, \quad \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{\text{NIV}}] = 0

The error variances are estimated on a validation set where human ratings are available.

F.3 Hypothesis Testing

H1 Test: Paired t-test comparing DINA vs. baseline on  \hat{O}  and  \widehat{\text{NIV}}  across stimuli. Use Bonferroni correction for two outcomes,  \alpha = 0.025  each. Report effect size (Cohen's d).

H2 Test: Bootstrap test on hypervolume difference. Compute  \Delta V = V(\mathcal{F}_{\text{IPN}}^{\text{DINA}}) - V(\mathcal{F}_{\text{IPN}}^{\text{Baseline}}) . Resample stimuli 10,000 times, compute 95% CI for  \Delta V . Reject null if CI excludes zero.

H3 Test: Paired comparison of attractor strength before/after escape. Estimate  A(a \mid S, \mathcal{M}_{\text{before}})  and  A(a \mid S, \mathcal{M}_{\text{after}})  via repeated sampling. Use Wilcoxon signed-rank test (non-parametric, since distribution may be skewed).

F.4 Power Analysis

For H1: with  \alpha = 0.025 , power = 0.8, expected effect size  d = 0.5 , required  n = 44 . Use  n = 50  stimuli.

For H2: Bootstrap power depends on effect size distribution; simulation recommended.

