Appendix H: Error Taxonomy

H.1 Grounding Errors

Error Type Description Example
Overgeneralization Inferring too much from visual evidence Inferring "nurse" from scrubs when person could be doctor
Under-detection Missing present facts Failing to detect visible injury
Bias in inference Inferring based on demographic priors Inferring "female" from nurse role
Confidence miscalibration Assigning wrong confidence conf(relaxed)=0.9 when posture ambiguous

H.2 Attractor Detection Errors

Error Type Description Example
False positive Flagging valid constraint as attractor Flagging "sunglasses exist" as attractor
False negative Missing genuine attractor Failing to detect "nurse → female"
Cross-cultural blindness Missing culturally specific attractors Failing to detect non-Western cliché

H.3 Verifier Errors

Error Type Description Example
Self-consistency trap Accepting internally consistent but incorrect propositions Accepting "sky is green" if narrative maintains it consistently
Sycophantic agreement Agreeing with generator's output Verifier passes an NIV because generator produced it
Over-penalization Flagging valid speculation as NIV Flagging "ocean is gateway" because speculative

H.4 Meta-Creative Errors

Error Type Description Example
Over-divergence Always diverging, never engaging attractors Rejecting perfect genre convention because familiar
Under-divergence Never diverging, always following attractors Always generating "lost object" narratives
Contrarianism Diverging in predictable ways Always selecting most absurd branch, which becomes new attractor

