Appendix L: Glossary

Artificial Hivemind: Phenomenon where LLMs produce highly similar outputs within and across models due to shared training data and RLHF alignment.

Attractor Basin: Region of probability landscape where a specific continuation has disproportionately high probability.

Attractor Strength: Model-relative measure  A(a \mid S, \mathcal{M}) .

Conceptual Distance:  d_c(p_i, p_j)  measuring difference in causal structure, entities, genre, etc.

Epistemic Classification:  \Phi_S(q)  assigning one of six categories.

Fidelity Violation: Contradicting observed facts.

Integrity-Preserving Novelty Frontier:  \mathcal{F}_{\text{IPN}} .

Load-Bearing Proposition: Proposition whose removal changes central narrative move.

Marked Speculation: Proposition under modal operator.

Narrative Integrity Violation (NIV): Unsupported, load-bearing, unmarked proposition altering ontology.

Typed Possibility Space:  \mathcal{W}_S .

Integrity Score:  I(N) = 1/(1+\text{NIV}(N)) .

Structural Contribution:  \Delta C_a .

Grounded Fact Base:  S = (S_{\text{obs}}, S_{\text{inf}}, S_{\text{unk}}) .

